All client-side TypeScript implementations must comply with ARIA (Accessible Rich Internet Applications) standards and WCAG guidelines. All shadcn/ui components must include proper accessibility attributes.

### shadcn/ui Button Component with ARIA

```typescript
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"

// Close button with aria-label
<Button 
  variant="ghost" 
  size="icon"
  aria-label="Close dialog"
  onClick={handleClose}
>
  ✕
</Button>

// Icon button with aria-label
<Button 
  variant="outline" 
  size="icon"
  aria-label="Toggle dark mode"
  aria-pressed={isDarkMode}
  onClick={toggleDarkMode}
>
  <MoonIcon className="h-4 w-4" />
</Button>

// Loading button with aria-busy
<Button 
  disabled={isLoading}
  aria-busy={isLoading}
  aria-label={isLoading ? "Submitting form..." : "Submit form"}
>
  {isLoading ? "Loading..." : "Submit"}
</Button>
```

### shadcn/ui Input Component with ARIA

```typescript
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input"
import { Label } from "@/components/ui/label"

// Email input with validation
<div className="space-y-2">
  <Label htmlFor="email">Email Address *</Label>
  <Input 
    id="email"
    type="email"
    placeholder="your@email.com"
    aria-label="Email address"
    aria-required="true"
    aria-invalid={hasEmailError}
    aria-describedby={hasEmailError ? "email-error" : undefined}
    disabled={isLoading}
  />
  {hasEmailError && (
    <span id="email-error" role="alert" className="text-sm text-red-600">
      Please enter a valid email address
    </span>
  )}
</div>

// Search input
<Input 
  type="search"
  placeholder="Search products..."
  aria-label="Search products by name or SKU"
  onChange={handleSearch}
/>
```

