### Minimum Requirements Checklist for shadcn/ui

- ✓ All `Button` components have `aria-label` when icon-only or contain only icon
- ✓ All `Input` components have associated `Label` with `htmlFor` or `aria-label`
- ✓ Required fields have `aria-required="true"`
- ✓ Invalid fields have `aria-invalid="true"` and `aria-describedby`
- ✓ `Dialog` components have `aria-labelledby` and `aria-describedby`
- ✓ `Tabs` have proper `role="tablist"`, `role="tab"`, and `role="tabpanel"`
- ✓ `Alert` components have `role="alert"` or `role="status"` with `aria-live`
- ✓ `Card` components wrapping articles have `role="article"` and `aria-labelledby`
- ✓ `Select` components have `aria-label` and `aria-required` when needed
- ✓ Interactive elements trigger `aria-busy` during loading states

### ARIA Roles Reference for shadcn Components

| Component | Primary Role | ARIA Attributes |
|-----------|--------------|-----------------|
| Button | button | aria-label, aria-pressed, aria-busy, aria-disabled |
| Input | textbox | aria-label, aria-required, aria-invalid, aria-describedby |
| Select | combobox | aria-label, aria-required, aria-expanded |
| Dialog | dialog | aria-labelledby, aria-describedby, aria-modal |
| Tabs | tablist/tab/tabpanel | role, aria-selected, aria-controls |
| Alert | alert/status | role, aria-live, aria-atomic |
| Card | article/region | aria-labelledby, aria-describedby |
| Badge | status | aria-label |

### aria-live Values in shadcn Context

- `polite` - Use for success messages and status updates (default in Toast)
- `assertive` - Use for error alerts and urgent warnings (destructive Toast)
- `off` - Use for non-urgent UI updates (default)

### Best Practices with shadcn/ui

1. **Use Label component**: Always pair `Input` with shadcn `Label` using `htmlFor`
2. **Semantic structure**: Use `Card`, `Dialog`, and `Alert` components as provided
3. **FormField wrapper**: Always use shadcn `FormField` with proper field configuration
4. **Icon accessibility**: Always provide `aria-label` for icon-only buttons
5. **Error handling**: Use `FormMessage` with `role="alert"` for validation errors
6. **Loading states**: Use `aria-busy` on buttons and `aria-live` on status messages
7. **Test with screen readers**: Verify shadcn components with NVDA/VoiceOver

### Testing Standards

- Validate against WCAG 2.1 Level AA standards
- Test shadcn components with at least one screen reader (NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver)
- Use browser accessibility inspector to verify ARIA tree
- Ensure keyboard navigation works for all interactive shadcn elements
- Verify `Tab` order through components
